{:edb/db-before-t 2602 :edb/db-after-t 2603 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535915 50 #inst "2026-10-09T10:35:20.152Z" 13194139535915 true] [17592186192579 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374171 13194139535915 true] [17592186192580 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374178 13194139535915 true] [17592186192580 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374185 13194139535915 true] [17592186192580 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374192 13194139535915 true] [17592186193219 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535915 true] [17592186193219 1100 "Compute $P(X > 8)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$f(x) = {\\frac{3}{x^{2}},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 3, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}x < 3$." 13194139535915 false] [17592186193219 1100 "Compute $P(X>8)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}},\\, & x\\ge 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535915 true] [17592186193219 1145 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>8) & =P(8<X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{3}{x}]}_{8}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374171 1017 #edb/ref 17592186374172 13194139535915 true] [17592186374171 1089 "q-126028" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374171 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535915 true] [17592186374171 1100 "Compute $P(X>4)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}},\\, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374171 1113 #uuid "8a8288b7-1b74-51d1-8dcd-4f3fd1e567da" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374171 1145 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>4) & =P(4<X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}]}_{4}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374173 13194139535915 true] [17592186374172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374174 13194139535915 true] [17592186374172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374175 13194139535915 true] [17592186374172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374176 13194139535915 true] [17592186374172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374177 13194139535915 true] [17592186374172 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535915 true] [17592186374172 1041 "selection" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374172 1104 #edb/ref 17592186374174 13194139535915 true] [17592186374172 1110 #uuid "f94390df-b864-5748-b687-817958347222" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374173 1034 "\\frac{1}{8}" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374173 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535915 true] [17592186374173 1111 #uuid "bd63c9c6-20ed-5696-a999-6cc866d8a7f7" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374174 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374174 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535915 true] [17592186374174 1111 #uuid "7c3c479b-be33-5f1b-a923-05ac65413c69" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374175 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374175 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535915 true] [17592186374175 1111 #uuid "f53980c9-858f-5bb0-8e8a-20ea6d296937" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374176 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374176 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535915 true] [17592186374176 1111 #uuid "fe9d5351-0a1d-5d28-a4be-15f1b1f4d661" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374177 1034 "\\frac{3}{8}" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374177 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535915 true] [17592186374177 1111 #uuid "3ac79523-07c8-5f5a-af0a-98899b46c7c1" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374178 1017 #edb/ref 17592186374179 13194139535915 true] [17592186374178 1089 "q-160464" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374178 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535915 true] [17592186374178 1100 "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{(2x-1)^{2}},\\, & x\\ge 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374178 1113 #uuid "0b864e29-79e4-5525-91aa-ed335a53cd91" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374178 1145 "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=\\frac{k}{(2x-1)^{2}}$ on the interval $x\\ge 2,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{k}{(2x-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }\\frac{k}{(2x-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{k}{2(2x-1)}\\,{|}_{2}^{\\infty }=\\frac{k}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{k}{6}=1\\,⟹\\,k=6.\n$$" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374180 13194139535915 true] [17592186374179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374181 13194139535915 true] [17592186374179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374182 13194139535915 true] [17592186374179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374183 13194139535915 true] [17592186374179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374184 13194139535915 true] [17592186374179 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535915 true] [17592186374179 1041 "selection" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374179 1104 #edb/ref 17592186374183 13194139535915 true] [17592186374179 1110 #uuid "cc7dacca-dfa0-5b83-98e9-4315fbaa0fc8" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374180 1034 "12" 13194139535915 true] [17592186374180 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 